; WHO 22 sound diffusion: the parameter forms of a command a gateway forwards on the amplifier
; 3#1#1: WHAT#P#1 and WHAT#4#P for WHAT 0 and 1, and WHAT#P for WHAT 3 and 4.
; Boundary probe of 2026-11-16 and 2026-11-17 on the 13 emulated gateways: P 0..20, 50, 99,
; 100, 255, 256, 1000 in every series; the WHAT#4#P series have no P = 1. The same forms for
; WHAT 35 are in sound-who22-what-parameters-35. The same forms for WHAT 34 are left out on
; purpose: on the MH202 they do not give a reproducible row (the two bus telegrams of
; *22*34#4#P*3#1#1## come in a changing order, in one of two runs the gateway answered nothing
; after *22*34#4#7*3#1#1##, and several of the forms get no reply at all).
;
; Result (stock settings, two identical runs per target, 13 targets): per group below, the
; gateways that forward the frame to the bus or answer it on the event session, and the
; gateways whose daemon crashes. Gateways not named drop the frame.

; 1. *22*0#N#1*3#1#1##
;    forwarded by 3488, F453, F453AV, F454, F459, F460, F461, MH200N, MH202, MyHomeServer1
